Most screen-time apps answer two questions: should you open this app, and how long should you stay. We compared the main Clearspace alternatives on exactly that: when each steps in, how strict it gets, what it costs, and where it runs, using only the apps' own listings, checked 24 November 2026.

One research detail stood out. In a preregistered PNAS experiment on one sec, the deliberation message alone had no significant effect. The plain option to dismiss did most of the work. Intention prompts turning into autopilot taps is predictable, not a personal failing.

What none of these tools address is how you feel 15 minutes into a session. That gap is why we are building DeRot, a mid-scroll breathing reset. It is not ranked in the comparison, and it is coming soon to iOS. {url}
